Neui is an AI agent and a web framework built as one stack. The core is a server-driven Go web framework (<a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;doors-dev&#x2F;doors" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;doors-dev&#x2F;doors</a>); neui (<a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;doors-dev&#x2F;neui" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;doors-dev&#x2F;neui</a>) turns each page into an agent harness.<p>FEATURES:<p><i>The agent sees &amp; operates UI.</i>
Annotate what agent can access (links, inputs, buttons), so agent sees it and can assist user with UI operations or even automate it with scripting.<p><pre><code>   ~&gt;neui.Use{ Desc:&quot;submit the form&quot; } &lt;button&gt;Submit&lt;&#x2F;button&gt;
</code></pre>
or expose context data for the agent:<p><pre><code>   &lt;div class=&quot;card&quot;&gt;
       ~neui.Data{Text: &quot;the product shown in the card&quot;, Object: product}
       ...
   &lt;&#x2F;div&gt;

</code></pre>
<i>Dynamic tools, right in the markup</i><p>Same way as you render a button to the user, you give the agent a tool. No endpoints or lifecycle management needed.<p><pre><code>  ~(if user.IsAdmin() {
      ~neui.Tool[Refund, Receipt]{
          Name: &quot;refund&quot;,
          Desc: &quot;Refund the order&quot;,
          Handler: orders.Refund,
      }
  })
</code></pre>
<i>Work environment</i><p>Isolated file workspaces and sandboxed scripting (&quot;code mode&quot;) out of the box.<p><i>Agentic apps</i><p>When a user needs something your UI doesn&#x27;t have, agent builds it on demand.<p>Complete chat experience<p>Thread list, history, message edits, full-text search, a message queue and automatic compaction.<p>Batteries included<p>MCP connector, web search and .xlsx tools, rich building blocks library for generative apps.<p>COMPARED TO COPILOT KIT:<p>- Agent thread runs on the server, so browser can&#x27;t rewrite the history&#x2F;tools to use your LLM backend + less traffic and faster tool-loops<p>- System prompt and provided tool list do not change during operation - it caches and stays hot (because it&#x27;s usually the same for all your users!)<p>- Pull-based, targeted UI sync; agent monitors only parts of UI that are relevant to the task (compared to full state attached to any user message)<p>- Neui is already a harness with its own sandbox - just bring your model.<p>- For generative UI agent writes a small app on specialized micro framework; agent doesn&#x27;t need to answer each click or load user input&#x2F;API responses into context<p>- CON: Is not stack-agnostic, like AG-UI stuff<p>TRY IT:<p>The repo has a demo app with all of this:<p><pre><code>  git clone https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;doors-dev&#x2F;neui &amp;&amp; cd neui
  DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=... go run .&#x2F;examples&#x2F;business-systems&#x2F;backoffice
</code></pre>
Then open http:&#x2F;&#x2F;localhost:8095. Claude, GPT, Gemini, DeepSeek and any OpenAI-compatible provider will work.<p>STATUS:<p>Both doors and neui are Apache-2.0. I released the first version about 3 weeks ago, so it&#x27;s early and I am still optimizing some system instructions. Neui itself took me 3 months, on top of the 2 years I spent on the framework underneath (it&#x27;s awesome, btw), which made it possible.
